== ROBIN ==

Small desk calculator, inspired by Ivy.
Rust.

Rules:
1. No operator precedence, right-associative ops.
2. Results are exact until an irrational op.
3. Whitespace non-significant.

Syntax:
Unary (abs x) and binary (pow x y), binary infix (x pow y)
Sugar wrappers: mul x y == x * y
No precedence. 2*3+4 = 14, not 10
Brackets to override. (2*3)+4 = 10

Numeric tower:
Int         i64
BigInt
BigRat      stored reduced
BigFloat    inexact. sqrt, log, exp, etc.

Promotion:
Every binary op (a op b) lifts a and b to max(a, b) for the computation,
the result takes the form it needs, and then may be demoted.
(3.5 mul 2) -> (3.5 mul 2.0) -> 7.0
(1 div 3)   -> 1r3
(4 div 2)   -> 2r1 -> 2

Demotion:
BigInt -> Int       OK, iff it fits
BigRat -> BigInt    OK, iff denom == 1      3r1 == 3
BigFloat -> *       NO

Equality:
Promotion only. 1 == 1.0 == 1r1
No boolean type just 0/1

Exactness:
BigFloat is a one-way operation.
Can only be produced with
    sqrt, log, exp
    trig + hyperbolic + inverse fns
    pow with non-integer exponent
    pi, euler
    float (conversion op)
    promotion
Exact is tried first. sqrt 4 -> 2.0 -> 2.
Decimal literals are exact. 1.234 = 1234r1000
2e5 == 200000
1e-3 == 1r1000

Literals:
Self-delimiting.
999         Base 10
0x30        Base 16
0b10101     Base 2
2e5         exponent
1.234       decimal
1r3         rational (note: / is always division)
1j2         reserved for future

- is always an operator. Exception as part of an exponent: 1e-3

Out of scope:
Lists
Matrix
Complex

